Package: baxters-aismartguy
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Baxters Lab <165753632+Baxterv5@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libjavascriptcoregtk-4.1-0,
 libsoup-3.0-0, libgtk-3-0t64, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0, libglib2.0-0t64, libcairo2
Description: AiSmartGuy — local AI assistant with a structured findings pipeline
 A desktop assistant built on Tauri and WebKitGTK. The interface is served from
 static files inside the package; there is no bundled model and nothing is
 fetched at install time.
 .
 Depends are exactly the binary's DIRECT NEEDED entries, resolved to their
 Ubuntu packages. libpango was in an earlier draft and is removed: it is pulled
 in by GTK rather than linked here, and a dependency list should say what this
 package needs, not what it happens to get. WebKitGTK and its
 JavaScriptCore and libsoup companions are the substance of a Tauri app on
 Linux: without them the package installs cleanly and then cannot open a window.
 .
 MIT licence added 2026-09-24 on the operator's instruction; this tree had none.
